---
# Copy this file to .claude/cc-opencode-cmux.local.md (project root) and adjust.
# Values here are read as environment variables by the plugin's bin/ scripts.

# Port for `opencode serve`. Default 4096.
port: 4096

# Hostname. Stay on loopback unless you know what you are doing.
host: 127.0.0.1

# Auto-start the serve daemon on SessionStart. Costs one idle daemon but saves
# the ensure-on-first-call latency (~1–3s).
auto_start: false
---

# cc-opencode-cmux local settings

This file is git-ignored. Use it for per-machine overrides. The plugin's `bin/`
scripts read these as env vars: `CC_OC_PORT`, `CC_OC_HOST`, `CC_OC_AUTOSTART`.
You can also export them in your shell profile instead of using this file.

> v0.5.0 dropped the right-split cmux pane. The `CC_OC_KEEP_SURFACE` /
> `keep_surface` setting no longer exists.

## Authentication

OC Zen and OC Go are **two separate OpenCode subscriptions**. Subscribing to one
does not unlock the other. Both end up authenticated under `OPENCODE_API_KEY` —
`opencode auth login` runs through a TUI menu where you choose which one.

### OpenCode Go ($10/month flat, 14 models)

```bash
opencode auth login   # menu: choose "OpenCode Go"
```

Models reachable via `opencode-go/<id>` (see `config/opencode.json.template` for
plugin-defined agent → model mappings):

- DeepSeek V4 Flash (31,650 req/5h, ctx 1M — biggest Go quota)
- Qwen 3.5 Plus (10,200 req/5h, ctx 256K)
- DeepSeek V4 Pro (3,450 req/5h, ctx 1M)
- Qwen 3.6 Plus (3,300 req/5h, ctx 256K — best Korean within Go)
- Kimi K2.6 (1,150 req/5h, ctx 256K — SWE-Bench Pro leader)
- (and several more)

### OpenCode Zen (pay-per-token, premium models)

```bash
opencode auth login   # menu: choose "OpenCode Zen"
```

Models reachable via `opencode/<id>`:

- `opencode/gemini-3-flash`, `opencode/gemini-3.1-pro`
- `opencode/claude-sonnet-4-5`, `opencode/claude-haiku-4-5`
- `opencode/gpt-5.1`, `opencode/gpt-5.4-mini`
- (and ~50 more — `opencode auth list` after login)

### BYOK (optional fallback)

Bypass the OC gateway. Set whichever you have:

- `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` — any `openrouter/...` model
- `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY`

> OpenCode does not support a `fallback_models` config field. Each agent in
> `config/opencode.json.template` lists alternative model IDs in its
> `description` for **manual** fallback — call the delegate-oc skill with a
> `--model <id>` hint in the spec, or override via Skill args.

## Verifying auth

```bash
opencode auth list
```

If at least one provider is listed (`opencode-go`, `opencode`, or a BYOK
provider), auth is in place.

## Overriding the daemon version

The plugin pins opencode to **v1.15.5** (see `bin/oc-daemon.sh PINNED_VERSION`).
If you need a different version, change that constant and restart the daemon —
but be aware of the known regressions documented in the project README.
